  "name": "5 NUCIEOTIDASE (5NT)",
  "code": "1012",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"162\" data-end=\"725\">The <strong data-start=\"166\" data-end=\"192\">5'-Nucleotidase (5-NT)</strong> test measures the activity of the 5'-nucleotidase enzyme in the blood. This enzyme is primarily found in the <strong data-start=\"302\" data-end=\"311\">liver</strong> and is involved in purine metabolism (specifically the breakdown of nucleotides). The test is used mainly to evaluate <strong data-start=\"430\" data-end=\"448\">liver function</strong>, especially to help <strong data-start=\"469\" data-end=\"536\">differentiate the source of elevated alkaline phosphatase (ALP)</strong> levels. Since both ALP and 5-NT are elevated in liver disease but <strong data-start=\"603\" data-end=\"637\">only ALP rises in bone disease</strong>, measuring 5-NT helps determine if elevated ALP is due to <strong data-start=\"696\" data-end=\"722\">hepatic (liver) origin</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"727\" data-end=\"767\">It is especially useful in diagnosing:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"768\" data-end=\"945\">\n<li data-start=\"768\" data-end=\"814\">\n<p data-start=\"770\" data-end=\"814\"><strong data-start=\"770\" data-end=\"785\">Cholestasis</strong> (obstruction of bile flow)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"815\" data-end=\"881\">\n<p data-start=\"817\" data-end=\"881\"><strong data-start=\"817\" data-end=\"843\">Hepatocellular disease</strong> (e.g., hepatitis, liver metastases)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"882\" data-end=\"945\">\n<p data-start=\"884\" data-end=\"945\"><strong data-start=\"884\" data-end=\"915\">Infiltrative liver diseases</strong> (e.g., sarcoidosis, tumors)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
